                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Boston/Norton MA",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 6 at 9:14PM EST until November 6 at 11:30PM EST by NWS Boston/Norton MA",
                "description": "At 914 PM EST, local law enforcement reported thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain which has led to numerous road closures across Acushnet\nand New Bedford. Between 1.5 and 2.5 inches of rain have fallen.\nAdditional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2.5 inches are possible in the\nwarned area. Flash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Law enforcement reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nNew Bedford, Fall River, Plymouth, Dartmouth, Marion,\nMiddleborough, Wareham, Bourne, Fairhaven, Westport, Carver,\nLakeville, Acushnet, Freetown, Mattapoisett and Rochester.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nStay away or be swept away. River banks and culverts can become\nunstable and unsafe.\n\nPlease report observed flooding to local emergency services or law\nenforcement and request they pass this information to the National\nWeather Service when you can do so safely.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
